    "body": "Fixes #23958\n\nHooks that vite calls itself now set `plugin` and `hook` on whatever they throw, and the message gets the `[plugin]` prefix through `enhanceRollupError`.\n\nIf an error already has a `plugin` I've left it alone. That way a css plugin's error thrown from `ssrLoadModule` inside some framework's `configureServer` still points at the css plugin as an example.\n\n@sapphi-red I didn't touch dev `resolveId` / `load` / `transform` since those run once per module. Should those get it too, or is this fine for now? I wasn't too sure about perf. Or if it's needed? Well it might be needed since plugins can indeed throw there as well. But just asking first yea.\n\nUsed Claude 👍🏻. I decided what to do and how to do it and let it work on the code. Ofc, reviewed it myself afterwards.",
